        "mission_intent": "We need to stand up a focused collection effort against Mexico-based transnational criminal organizations\u2014specifically Sinaloa Cartel and CJNG\u2014to monitor anticipated shifts in drug smuggling techniques and routing in response to the heightened U.S. security posture along the southwest border. The 2025 threat assessment highlights that official ports of entry have been the primary vector for fentanyl and other synthetics, typically concealed in passenger vehicles and commercial tractor trailers, but we expect TCOs to adapt their tradecraft at least temporarily. I'm requesting HUMINT and SIGINT tasking nominations through the National Collection Coordination process to detect early indicators of route diversification\u2014whether that means increased use of unofficial crossings, maritime approaches, or tunneling activity. Coordinate with DEA SOD and CBP intelligence for deconfliction and ensure any nominations reference existing NIPF priority frameworks for counternarcotics. We also need periodic reporting to capture changes in precursor chemical sourcing from PRC-based suppliers that feed into Mexican fentanyl production. Please have initial tasking nominations drafted and routed for approval by end of next week so we can brief the interagency working group the following Monday.",
